<title>USA: Payless Cashways Inc Q3 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Payless Cashways Inc Q3 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.61   profit	$ 0.17</p>
<p> Net loss		  22,878   profit	 8,146</p>
<p> Revs		     723,793		  737,237</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  39,952		   40,116</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Periods ended August 24 vs August 26.</p>
<p>EBIDTA profit $31.9 million vs $48.9 million.</p>
<p>1996 Q3 results include pre-tax charges of $73.7 million from planned store closings and accounting change.  </p>
<p>		  9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.73   profit	$ 0.12</p>
<p> Net loss		  24,635   profit	 8,895</p>
<p> Revs		   1,932,812		2,005,134</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  39,939		   39,969</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Nine months EBITDA profit $85.3 million vs $115.5 million.</p>
<p>1996 Q3 results included $23.7 million income tax benefit and $4.9 million of related interest income due to recent legislation and an Internal Revenue Service settlement.  </p>
<p>Without the non-routine items recorded in the Q3, net income for 1996 would have been $3.6 million or $0.05/shr.</p>
<p>Excluding non-routine items for the 1996 nine months, the net loss would have been $0.06/shr.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
